    "# MyBinder.org Setup for Java\n",
    "\n",
    "**To run this notebook on MyBinder.org, your repository needs a configuration file to tell MyBinder how to build the Java environment.**\n",
    "\n",
    "1.  **Create a file named `Dockerfile`** in the root of your GitHub repository.\n",
    "2.  **Copy the following content** into the `Dockerfile`:\n",
    "\n",
    "    ```Dockerfile\n",
    "    FROM jupyter/base-notebook:latest\n",
    "\n",
    "    USER root\n",
    "    RUN apt-get update && \\n",
    "        apt-get install -y openjdk-21-jdk && \\n",
    "        apt-get clean && \\n",
    "        rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*\n",
    "    USER ${NB_UID}\n",
    "\n",
    "    RUN wget https://github.com/SpencerPark/IJava/releases/download/v1.3.0/ijava-1.3.0.zip && \\n",
    "        unzip ijava-1.3.0.zip && \\n",
    "        python3 install.py --sys-prefix && \\n",
    "        rm ijava-1.3.0.zip\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Add notebook files\n",
    "    COPY --chown=${NB_UID}:${NB_GID} . /home/${NB_USER}/work\n",
    "    ```\n",
    "\n",
    "3.  Commit and push the `Dockerfile` to your repository.\n",
    "4.  Go to [mybinder.org](https://mybinder.org/), enter your repository URL, and launch the environment.\n",
    "\n",
    "This `Dockerfile` installs Java 21 and the IJava kernel, which allows Jupyter to execute Java code."
   ]
  },
