    "# Mastering Modern Java: From Functional to Advanced (Java 8 to 21) - Enhanced Edition\n",
    "\n",
    "This comprehensive training is designed for developers with some existing Java knowledge who are ready to embrace the modern, expressive, and powerful features introduced from Java 8 up to Java 21. Each module is crafted to be a deep dive into a core concept, complete with detailed explanations, best practices, and multiple hands-on code examples."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Module 1: Functional Interfaces & Lambdas (Java 8+)\n",
    "**Goal:** Transition from verbose anonymous inner classes to concise, readable, and functional code. This is the foundational skill for modern Java.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1.1 What is a Functional Interface?\n",
    "A functional interface is any interface that has **exactly one abstract method**. This constraint allows it to be the target for a lambda expression or a method reference. The `@FunctionalInterface` annotation is optional but recommended, as it tells the compiler to enforce this rule.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1.2 The \"Core Four\" Functional Interfaces: A Deep Dive\n",
    "These four interfaces are the bread and butter of functional programming in Java.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### 1. **`Predicate<T>`**:\n",
    "*   **Signature**: `boolean test(T t)`\n",
    "*   **Purpose**: To test a condition. Think of it as a \"filter\" or a \"matcher.\"\n",
    "*   **Example**: From Anonymous Class to Lambda"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "// Before: Anonymous Class\n",
    "import java.util.function.Predicate;\n",
    "Predicate<String> isLong = new Predicate<String>() {\n",
    "    @Override\n",
    "    public boolean test(String s) {\n",
    "        return s.length() > 10;\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "\n",
    "// After: Lambda Expression\n",
    "Predicate<String> isLongLambda = s -> s.length() > 10;\n",
    "System.out.println(\"Is 'hello' a long string? \" + isLongLambda.test(\"hello\"));\n",
    "System.out.println(\"Is 'introduction' a long string? \" + isLongLambda.test(\"introduction\"));"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 2. **`Function<T, R>`**:\n",
    "*   **Signature**: `R apply(T t)`\n",
    "*   **Purpose**: To transform data. It takes an object of type `T` and returns an object of type `R`.\n",
    "*   **Example**: From Anonymous Class to Lambda"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "// Before: Anonymous Class\n",
    "import java.util.function.Function;\n",
    "Function<String, Integer> getLength = new Function<String, Integer>() {\n",
    "    @Override\n",
    "    public Integer apply(String s) {\n",
    "        return s.length();\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "\n",
    "// After: Lambda Expression\n",
    "Function<String, Integer> getLengthLambda = s -> s.length();\n",
    "System.out.println(\"Length of 'world': \" + getLengthLambda.apply(\"world\"));"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 3. **`Consumer<T>`**:\n",
    "*   **Signature**: `void accept(T t)`\n",
    "*   **Purpose**: To perform an action with an object without returning anything (a \"side effect\").\n",
    "*   **Example**: From Anonymous Class to Lambda"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "// Before: Anonymous Class\n",
    "import java.util.function.Consumer;\n",
    "Consumer<String> printUpperCase = new Consumer<String>() {\n",
    "    @Override\n",
    "    public void accept(String s) {\n",
    "        System.out.println(s.toUpperCase());\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "\n",
    "// After: Lambda Expression\n",
    "Consumer<String> printUpperCaseLambda = s -> System.out.println(s.toUpperCase());\n",
    "printUpperCaseLambda.accept(\"hello world\");"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "#### 4. **`Supplier<T>`**:\n",
    "*   **Signature**: `T get()`\n",
    "*   **Purpose**: To produce or provide a value without taking any input. Think of it as a \"factory.\"\n",
    "*   **Example**: From Anonymous Class to Lambda"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "// Before: Anonymous Class\n",
    "import java.util.function.Supplier;\n",
    "Supplier<String> greeting = new Supplier<String>() {\n",
    "    @Override\n",
    "    public String get() {\n",
    "        return \"Hello from Supplier!\";\n",
    "    }\n",
    "};\n",
    "\n",
    "// After: Lambda Expression\n",
    "Supplier<String> greetingLambda = () -> \"Hello from Supplier!\";\n",
    "System.out.println(greetingLambda.get());"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.3 Method References (`::`)\n",
    "Method references are a shorthand for lambdas that simply call an existing method. They make code even more readable by focusing on the method's name.\n",
    "\n",
    "*   **Static method reference**: `ClassName::staticMethodName`\n",
    "*   **Instance method reference on a particular object**: `instance::instanceMethodName`\n",
    "*   **Instance method reference on an arbitrary object of a particular type**: `ClassName::instanceMethodName`\n",
    "*   **Constructor reference**: `ClassName::new`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import java.util.List;\n",
    "import java.util.stream.Collectors;\n",
    "\n",
    "List<String> names = List.of(\"anna\", \"bob\", \"charlie\");\n",
    "\n",
    "// Lambda: s -> System.out.println(s)\n",
    "// Method Reference:\n",
    "names.forEach(System.out::println);\n",
    "\n",
    "// Lambda: s -> s.toUpperCase()\n",
    "// Method Reference:\n",
    "List<String> upperCaseNames = names.stream()\n",
    "    .map(String::toUpperCase)\n",
    "    .collect(Collectors.toList());\n",
    "System.out.println(upperCaseNames);"
   ]
  },
